2026-07-16 first comparison-parser failure (preserved verbatim in substance)

The MATLAB backend completed all 12 cases with exit code 0. The first Python
post-processing pass then raised before writing the comparison CSV:

RuntimeError: MATLAB per-case failures: {
  'em_halo_12p40_n21': '[]',
  'em_halo_12p40_n33': '[]',
  'em_halo_12p40_n45': '[]',
  'em_vertical_12p66_n33': '[]',
  'em_vertical_12p66_n45': '[]',
  'em_vertical_12p66_n57': '[]',
  'se_active_geometry_member_468': '[]',
  'route_h_member_17': '[]',
  'route_h_member_32': '[]',
  'route_h_member_54': '[]',
  'route_h_member_68': '[]',
  'route_h_member_68_legacy_dg_positive': '[]'
}

Root cause: scipy.io.loadmat represented MATLAB empty character-array error
fields as zero-length arrays. The parser converted them to the nonempty text
"[]" and conservatively treated every case as failed. Recovery: recognize a
zero-length array as an empty error field, then rerun input preparation,
MATLAB Schur/ordschur, and the entire comparison. No numerical tolerance,
case selection, or source artifact changed.
